---
description: Core project constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read `AGENTS.md` and `project.config.ts` before starting.
- Keep work inside the requested scope and preserve unrelated changes.
- Treat project documents and current code as sources of truth.
- Use Astro and semantic HTML by default.
- Add client JavaScript only for real interaction.
- Do not add dependencies without a documented reason.
- Do not invent business, legal, product, or integration facts.
- Keep pages declarative and data separate from presentation.
- Type props and data without `any`.
- Reuse a real contract before creating a component or variant.
- Use Tailwind utilities for local composition.
- Keep shared tokens and base rules in `src/styles/globals.css`.
- Do not change global tokens for an isolated local issue.
- Do not perform opportunistic refactors.
- Use `astro:assets` for processable images.
- Preserve one `h1`, valid landmarks, focus, labels, and reduced motion.
- Run the checks routed by `docs/project/QA.md`.
- Inspect rendered UI after relevant visual work.
- Stop after two failed attempts on the same defect and report evidence.
